-- Post 1019: Understanding OBD Diagnostic Codes
UPDATE public.app_post SET 
    title = 'Understanding OBD Diagnostic Codes: A Beginner''s Guide',
    slug = 'understanding-obd-diagnostic-codes-beginners-guide',
    description = '<h3>What Are OBD Diagnostic Codes?</h3><p>On-Board Diagnostics (OBD) codes are standardized trouble codes that help identify vehicle problems. When your check engine light comes on, these codes provide specific information about what''s wrong with your vehicle.</p><h4>Common OBD Code Categories</h4><p><strong>P-Codes (Powertrain):</strong> Engine, transmission, and emission-related issues</p><p><strong>B-Codes (Body):</strong> Air conditioning, airbags, and body control modules</p><p><strong>C-Codes (Chassis):</strong> ABS, steering, and suspension systems</p><p><strong>U-Codes (Network):</strong> Communication between vehicle modules</p><h4>How to Read OBD Codes</h4><p>Every code follows a specific format: Letter + Number + Number + Number</p><p>Example: P0171 means "System Too Lean (Bank 1)"</p><h4>Common Diagnostic Tools</h4><ul><li><strong>Basic OBD2 Scanners:</strong> Read and clear codes ($20-50)</li><li><strong>Professional Tools:</strong> Launch X431 series for advanced diagnostics</li><li><strong>Smartphone Apps:</strong> Use Bluetooth OBD adapters</li></ul><h4>When to Seek Professional Help</h4><p>While basic code reading is helpful, complex issues require professional diagnosis. At Logivis, we provide expert OBD diagnostic services with advanced tools to accurately identify and resolve vehicle problems.</p><p>📞 Need professional OBD diagnostics? Contact Logivis for expert vehicle analysis across Sri Lanka.</p>',
    status = 'published'
WHERE id = 1019;

-- Post 1020: Top 5 Automotive Tools
UPDATE public.app_post SET 
    title = 'Top 5 Automotive Tools Every Car Owner Should Have',
    slug = 'top-5-automotive-tools-every-car-owner-should-have',
    description = '<h3>Essential Tools for Basic Car Maintenance</h3><p>Every car owner should have these fundamental tools for basic maintenance and emergency situations:</p><h4>1. OBD2 Scanner</h4><p><strong>Why You Need It:</strong> Diagnose check engine lights and monitor vehicle performance</p><p><strong>Recommended:</strong> Launch CReader series or basic Bluetooth adapters</p><p><strong>Price Range:</strong> LKR 3,000 - 25,000</p><h4>2. Socket Set with Ratchet</h4><p><strong>Essential Sizes:</strong> 8mm, 10mm, 12mm, 13mm, 14mm, 17mm, 19mm</p><p><strong>Use:</strong> Oil changes, tire rotations, basic repairs</p><p><strong>Quality Brands:</strong> Craftsman, Tekton, or local quality sets</p><h4>3. Digital Multimeter</h4><p><strong>Functions:</strong> Test battery voltage, check fuses, diagnose electrical issues</p><p><strong>Features to Look For:</strong> Auto-ranging, continuity test, DC/AC voltage</p><h4>4. Tire Pressure Gauge & Portable Compressor</h4><p><strong>Importance:</strong> Proper tire pressure improves fuel economy and safety</p><p><strong>Tip:</strong> Check pressure monthly, especially before long trips</p><h4>5. Basic Hand Tools</h4><ul><li>Screwdriver set (Phillips and flathead)</li><li>Pliers (needle-nose and standard)</li><li>Adjustable wrench</li><li>Flashlight or headlamp</li></ul><h4>Bonus: Emergency Kit</h4><ul><li>Jumper cables</li><li>Emergency triangle</li><li>First aid kit</li><li>Basic fluids (engine oil, brake fluid)</li></ul><p>💡 <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Start with basic tools and upgrade as you gain experience. Quality tools last longer and perform better.</p><p>🔧 Looking for professional-grade automotive tools? Logivis offers quality diagnostic equipment and hand tools for both DIY enthusiasts and professional mechanics.</p>',
    status = 'published'
WHERE id = 1020;

-- Post 1021: Choosing Right Engine Oil
UPDATE public.app_post SET 
    title = 'How to Choose the Right Engine Oil for Your Vehicle',
    slug = 'how-to-choose-right-engine-oil-for-your-vehicle',
    description = '<h3>Understanding Engine Oil Basics</h3><p>Choosing the correct engine oil is crucial for vehicle performance, fuel economy, and engine longevity. Here''s your complete guide to making the right choice.</p><h4>Oil Viscosity Ratings Explained</h4><p><strong>What Do Numbers Mean?</strong></p><ul><li><strong>0W-20:</strong> Thin oil, better fuel economy, newer engines</li><li><strong>5W-30:</strong> Most common, good all-weather performance</li><li><strong>10W-40:</strong> Thicker oil, older engines, high-mileage vehicles</li><li><strong>15W-40:</strong> Heavy-duty applications, diesel engines</li></ul><h4>Oil Types Available</h4><p><strong>1. Conventional Oil</strong></p><ul><li>Cheapest option</li><li>Good for older vehicles</li><li>More frequent changes needed</li></ul><p><strong>2. Synthetic Blend</strong></p><ul><li>Better performance than conventional</li><li>Moderate price</li><li>Good compromise option</li></ul><p><strong>3. Full Synthetic</strong></p><ul><li>Best protection and performance</li><li>Longer change intervals</li><li>Higher upfront cost</li></ul><h4>Climate Considerations for Sri Lanka</h4><p><strong>Hot Weather Performance:</strong> Choose oils with good high-temperature stability</p><p><strong>Recommended for Tropical Climate:</strong> 5W-30 or 0W-20 for most modern vehicles</p><p><strong>High-Mileage Vehicles:</strong> Consider 10W-40 or high-mileage formulas</p><h4>Brand Recommendations</h4><ul><li><strong>Premium:</strong> Mobil 1, Castrol GTX, Shell Helix</li><li><strong>Good Value:</strong> Valvoline, Havoline, local quality brands</li><li><strong>Diesel Engines:</strong> Delo, Rotella, Castrol Diesel</li></ul><h4>Change Interval Guidelines</h4><ul><li><strong>Conventional Oil:</strong> Every 3,000-5,000 km</li><li><strong>Synthetic Blend:</strong> Every 5,000-7,500 km</li><li><strong>Full Synthetic:</strong> Every 7,500-10,000 km</li></ul><p><strong>Important:</strong> Always follow manufacturer recommendations in your owner''s manual.</p><p>🛠️ Need professional oil change service or oil recommendations for your specific vehicle? Contact Logivis for expert advice and quality service across Sri Lanka.</p>',
    status = 'published'
WHERE id = 1021;

-- Post 1022: EV Charging Infrastructure
UPDATE public.app_post SET 
    title = 'Electric Vehicle Charging Infrastructure in Sri Lanka: Current State and Future',
    slug = 'ev-charging-infrastructure-sri-lanka-current-state-future',
    description = '<h3>The Growing EV Charging Network in Sri Lanka</h3><p>As electric vehicles gain popularity in Sri Lanka, charging infrastructure development is accelerating. Here''s a comprehensive look at the current state and future prospects.</p><h4>Current Charging Network Status</h4><p><strong>Major Cities Coverage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Colombo:</strong> 25+ public charging stations</li><li><strong>Kandy:</strong> 8+ charging points</li><li><strong>Galle:</strong> 6+ stations along Southern Expressway</li><li><strong>Negombo:</strong> 4+ stations including airport area</li></ul><h4>Types of Charging Available</h4><p><strong>1. Level 1 (AC Slow Charging)</strong></p><ul><li>Power: 3.7kW</li><li>Time: 8-12 hours for full charge</li><li>Best for: Home charging, overnight parking</li></ul><p><strong>2. Level 2 (AC Fast Charging)</strong></p><ul><li>Power: 7kW - 22kW</li><li>Time: 3-6 hours for full charge</li><li>Location: Shopping malls, hotels, workplaces</li></ul><p><strong>3. DC Fast Charging</strong></p><ul><li>Power: 50kW - 150kW</li><li>Time: 30-60 minutes for 80% charge</li><li>Location: Highways, commercial areas</li></ul><h4>Major Charging Network Providers</h4><ul><li><strong>Ceylon Electricity Board (CEB)</strong></li><li><strong>PickMe Power</strong></li><li><strong>Shell Recharge</strong></li><li><strong>Private operators and hotels</strong></li></ul><h4>Government Initiatives</h4><p><strong>National Policy Support:</strong></p><ul><li>Tax incentives for EV purchases</li><li>Reduced import duties on EVs</li><li>Support for charging infrastructure development</li><li>Plans for 1,000+ charging points by 2026</li></ul><h4>Future Development Plans</h4><p><strong>2025-2027 Expansion:</strong></p><ul><li>Expressway charging corridors</li><li>Tourist destination charging hubs</li><li>Residential complex installations</li><li>Workplace charging programs</li></ul><h4>Challenges and Solutions</h4><p><strong>Current Challenges:</strong></p><ul><li>Limited rural coverage</li><li>Standardization of charging connectors</li><li>Grid capacity in remote areas</li></ul><p><strong>Upcoming Solutions:</strong></p><ul><li>Solar-powered charging stations</li><li>Battery storage integration</li><li>Smart grid technology</li></ul><h4>Cost of Charging</h4><ul><li><strong>Home charging:</strong> LKR 15-25 per kWh</li><li><strong>Public AC charging:</strong> LKR 25-35 per kWh</li><li><strong>DC fast charging:</strong> LKR 35-50 per kWh</li></ul><p>🔌 <strong>Planning to switch to electric?</strong> Contact Logivis for EV consultation, charging solutions, and diagnostic services to support your electric journey in Sri Lanka.</p>',
    status = 'published'
WHERE id = 1022;

-- Post 1023: Brake System Maintenance
UPDATE public.app_post SET 
    title = 'Brake System Maintenance: When to Replace Pads and Rotors',
    slug = 'brake-system-maintenance-when-replace-pads-rotors',
    description = '<h3>Essential Brake System Knowledge</h3><p>Your brake system is your vehicle''s most critical safety feature. Understanding when to replace brake components can prevent accidents and save money on repairs.</p><h4>Warning Signs Your Brakes Need Attention</h4><p><strong>Brake Pad Replacement Signs:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Squealing or squeaking noise</strong> when braking</li><li><strong>Grinding sound</strong> - immediate replacement needed</li><li><strong>Vibration in brake pedal</strong> during braking</li><li><strong>Longer stopping distances</strong></li><li><strong>Brake warning light</strong> on dashboard</li></ul><p><strong>Brake Rotor Issues:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pulsating brake pedal</strong></li><li><strong>Steering wheel shaking</strong> when braking</li><li><strong>Visible scoring or grooves</strong> on rotor surface</li><li><strong>Blue discoloration</strong> from overheating</li></ul><h4>Brake Component Lifespan</h4><p><strong>Brake Pads:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>City driving:</strong> 25,000-40,000 km</li><li><strong>Highway driving:</strong> 40,000-60,000 km</li><li><strong>Aggressive driving:</strong> 15,000-25,000 km</li></ul><p><strong>Brake Rotors:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Standard rotors:</strong> 50,000-80,000 km</li><li><strong>High-quality rotors:</strong> 80,000-120,000 km</li><li><strong>Performance rotors:</strong> 40,000-60,000 km</li></ul><h4>Types of Brake Pads</h4><p><strong>1. Organic (NAO - Non-Asbestos Organic)</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pros:</strong> Quiet, smooth, affordable</li><li><strong>Cons:</strong> Shorter lifespan, more brake dust</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Daily commuting, light use</li></ul><p><strong>2. Semi-Metallic</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pros:</strong> Good heat dissipation, longer lasting</li><li><strong>Cons:</strong> Noisier, harder on rotors</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Heavy-duty use, towing</li></ul><p><strong>3. Ceramic</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pros:</strong> Quiet, less dust, long-lasting</li><li><strong>Cons:</strong> More expensive</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Premium vehicles, performance cars</li></ul><h4>Brake Maintenance Schedule</h4><p><strong>Every 10,000 km:</strong></p><ul><li>Visual inspection of brake pads</li><li>Check brake fluid level</li><li>Test brake pedal feel</li></ul><p><strong>Every 20,000 km:</strong></p><ul><li>Measure pad thickness</li><li>Inspect brake lines and hoses</li><li>Check rotor condition</li></ul><p><strong>Every 40,000 km:</strong></p><ul><li>Brake fluid replacement</li><li>Complete brake system inspection</li><li>Clean and lubricate brake components</li></ul><h4>Brake Fluid Importance</h4><p><strong>Why Replace Brake Fluid:</strong></p><ul><li>Absorbs moisture over time</li><li>Reduced boiling point when contaminated</li><li>Can cause brake fade and system corrosion</li></ul><p><strong>Replacement Interval:</strong> Every 2-3 years or 40,000 km</p><h4>DIY vs Professional Service</h4><p><strong>DIY Suitable For:</strong></p><ul><li>Visual inspections</li><li>Checking brake fluid level</li><li>Basic pad thickness measurements</li></ul><p><strong>Professional Service Required:</strong></p><ul><li>Brake pad replacement</li><li>Rotor resurfacing or replacement</li><li>Brake fluid bleeding</li><li>Brake system diagnostics</li></ul><p>🔧 <strong>Brake issues are safety-critical!</strong> Don''t compromise on brake maintenance. Contact Logivis for professional brake system inspection, maintenance, and repair services across Sri Lanka.</p>',
    status = 'published'
WHERE id = 1023;

-- Post 1024: Fuel Efficiency Tips
UPDATE public.app_post SET 
    title = 'Fuel Efficiency Tips: Maximizing Your Vehicle''s MPG',
    slug = 'fuel-efficiency-tips-maximizing-vehicle-mpg',
    description = '<h3>Maximize Your Vehicle''s Fuel Economy</h3><p>With rising fuel costs in Sri Lanka, improving your vehicle''s fuel efficiency has become more important than ever. These proven techniques can help you save money and reduce environmental impact.</p><h4>Driving Techniques for Better Fuel Economy</h4><p><strong>1. Smooth Acceleration and Braking</strong></p><ul><li>Accelerate gradually to maintain steady speed</li><li>Anticipate traffic to avoid sudden stops</li><li>Use regenerative braking in hybrid vehicles</li><li>Potential savings: 10-15%</li></ul><p><strong>2. Maintain Steady Highway Speeds</strong></p><ul><li>Optimal speed: 80-90 km/h on highways</li><li>Use cruise control on flat terrain</li><li>Avoid excessive speeding (saves up to 20%)</li></ul><p><strong>3. Reduce Idling Time</strong></p><ul><li>Turn off engine for stops over 30 seconds</li><li>Use remote start wisely in hot weather</li><li>Modern engines don''t need long warm-up periods</li></ul><h4>Vehicle Maintenance for Fuel Efficiency</h4><p><strong>1. Regular Engine Maintenance</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Oil changes:</strong> Use recommended oil viscosity</li><li><strong>Air filter:</strong> Replace every 15,000-20,000 km</li><li><strong>Spark plugs:</strong> Replace per manufacturer schedule</li><li><strong>Fuel injector cleaning:</strong> Every 30,000 km</li></ul><p><strong>2. Tire Maintenance</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Proper pressure:</strong> Check monthly (saves 3-5%)</li><li><strong>Alignment:</strong> Annual check and adjustment</li><li><strong>Tire rotation:</strong> Every 10,000 km</li><li><strong>Quality tires:</strong> Low rolling resistance options</li></ul><p><strong>3. Transmission Service</strong></p><ul><li>Automatic transmission fluid changes</li><li>Manual transmission oil replacement</li><li>CVT maintenance per schedule</li></ul><h4>Planning and Route Optimization</h4><p><strong>Trip Planning:</strong></p><ul><li>Combine errands into single trips</li><li>Use GPS to find efficient routes</li><li>Avoid peak traffic hours when possible</li><li>Choose routes with fewer traffic lights</li></ul><p><strong>Load Management:</strong></p><ul><li>Remove unnecessary items from vehicle</li><li>Use roof racks only when needed</li><li>Keep windows closed at highway speeds</li></ul><h4>Technology and Fuel Economy</h4><p><strong>Fuel Economy Apps:</strong></p><ul><li>Track real-time fuel consumption</li><li>Monitor driving habits</li><li>Set efficiency goals and challenges</li></ul><p><strong>Vehicle Features to Use:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Eco mode:</strong> Optimizes engine and transmission</li><li><strong>Start/stop systems:</strong> Reduces idle fuel consumption</li><li><strong>Trip computers:</strong> Monitor real-time efficiency</li></ul><h4>Fuel Quality and Additives</h4><p><strong>Choose Quality Fuel:</strong></p><ul><li>Use reputable fuel stations</li><li>Consider premium fuel for high-performance engines</li><li>Avoid overfilling the tank</li></ul><p><strong>Fuel Additives:</strong></p><ul><li>Fuel injector cleaners (periodic use)</li><li>Fuel stabilizers for stored vehicles</li><li>Octane boosters for high-compression engines</li></ul><h4>Seasonal Considerations</h4><p><strong>Hot Weather (Sri Lankan Climate):</strong></p><ul><li>Use A/C efficiently (recirculate air)</li><li>Park in shade when possible</li><li>Maintain proper tire pressure (heat increases pressure)</li><li>Service cooling system regularly</li></ul><h4>Expected Fuel Savings</h4><ul><li><strong>Proper maintenance:</strong> 4-10% improvement</li><li><strong>Efficient driving:</strong> 10-20% improvement</li><li><strong>Route planning:</strong> 5-15% improvement</li><li><strong>Vehicle modifications:</strong> 2-8% improvement</li></ul><p><strong>Total Potential Savings: 20-40% with consistent application of all techniques</strong></p><p>⛽ <strong>Looking to optimize your vehicle''s fuel efficiency?</strong> Contact Logivis for professional engine tuning, maintenance services, and fuel system optimization across Sri Lanka.</p>',
    status = 'published'
WHERE id = 1024;

-- Post 1025: Vehicle Suspension Systems  
UPDATE public.app_post SET 
    title = 'Understanding Vehicle Suspension Systems and Common Problems',
    slug = 'understanding-vehicle-suspension-systems-common-problems',
    description = '<h3>Your Vehicle''s Suspension System Explained</h3><p>The suspension system is crucial for ride comfort, vehicle handling, and tire wear. Understanding how it works and recognizing problems early can save you money and improve safety.</p><h4>Components of Suspension Systems</h4><p><strong>1. Springs</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Coil springs:</strong> Most common, provide vertical support</li><li><strong>Leaf springs:</strong> Used in trucks and heavy-duty vehicles</li><li><strong>Torsion bars:</strong> Compact design for front suspensions</li><li><strong>Air springs:</strong> Adjustable, luxury and commercial vehicles</li></ul><p><strong>2. Shock Absorbers (Dampers)</strong></p><ul><li>Control spring oscillation</li><li>Provide stability during braking and turning</li><li>Types: Twin-tube, monotube, gas-charged</li></ul><p><strong>3. Struts</strong></p><ul><li>Combine spring and shock absorber</li><li>Structural component of suspension</li><li>Common in front suspension systems</li></ul><p><strong>4. Control Arms and Bushings</strong></p><ul><li>Connect wheels to vehicle frame</li><li>Allow controlled wheel movement</li><li>Rubber bushings provide cushioning</li></ul><h4>Common Suspension Problems</h4><p><strong>Worn Shock Absorbers/Struts Signs:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Bouncing:</strong> Vehicle continues bouncing after hitting bumps</li><li><strong>Nose diving:</strong> Front end dips during braking</li><li><strong>Swaying:</strong> Body roll during turns</li><li><strong>Uneven tire wear:</strong> Cupping or scalloping patterns</li><li><strong>Fluid leaks:</strong> Oil stains near shock absorbers</li></ul><p><strong>Spring Problems:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Sagging:</strong> Vehicle sits lower on one side</li><li><strong>Harsh ride:</strong> Broken or worn springs</li><li><strong>Clunking noises:</strong> Broken spring coils</li></ul><p><strong>Control Arm and Bushing Issues:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Steering wander:</strong> Vehicle pulls to one side</li><li><strong>Vibration:</strong> Felt through steering wheel</li><li><strong>Clunking sounds:</strong> Over bumps or during turning</li><li><strong>Uneven tire wear:</strong> Inner or outer edge wear</li></ul><h4>Suspension Maintenance Schedule</h4><p><strong>Every 20,000 km:</strong></p><ul><li>Visual inspection of all suspension components</li><li>Check for leaks, damage, or excessive wear</li><li>Test shock absorber bounce test</li></ul><p><strong>Every 40,000 km:</strong></p><ul><li>Detailed inspection of bushings and joints</li><li>Alignment check and adjustment</li><li>Replace worn suspension components</li></ul><p><strong>As Needed:</strong></p><ul><li>Replace shock absorbers: 50,000-100,000 km</li><li>Replace struts: 60,000-120,000 km</li><li>Replace bushings: 80,000-150,000 km</li></ul><h4>Types of Suspension Systems</h4><p><strong>1. Independent Front Suspension</strong></p><ul><li><strong>MacPherson strut:</strong> Common, compact design</li><li><strong>Double wishbone:</strong> Performance-oriented, better control</li><li><strong>Multi-link:</strong> Complex, excellent handling</li></ul><p><strong>2. Rear Suspension Types</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Independent:</strong> Better ride quality, more expensive</li><li><strong>Solid axle:</strong> Durable, used in trucks and SUVs</li><li><strong>Semi-independent:</strong> Compromise between cost and performance</li></ul><h4>Suspension Modifications and Upgrades</h4><p><strong>Performance Upgrades:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Sport shocks:</strong> Improved handling and control</li><li><strong>Lowering springs:</strong> Reduced body roll, sportier appearance</li><li><strong>Sway bars:</strong> Reduced body roll during cornering</li><li><strong>Coilover kits:</strong> Adjustable height and damping</li></ul><p><strong>Comfort Improvements:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Premium shocks:</strong> Better ride quality</li><li><strong>Air suspension:</strong> Adjustable ride height</li><li><strong>Electronic dampers:</strong> Adaptive suspension systems</li></ul><h4>Driving Conditions in Sri Lanka</h4><p><strong>Road Challenges:</strong></p><ul><li>Pothole damage to suspension components</li><li>Speed bumps causing premature wear</li><li>Monsoon water damage to bushings</li><li>Dust and debris affecting seals</li></ul><p><strong>Maintenance Tips:</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid potholes when safely possible</li><li>Slow down over speed bumps</li><li>Regular washing to remove corrosive elements</li><li>Professional inspection after impact damage</li></ul><h4>Cost of Suspension Repairs</h4><ul><li><strong>Shock absorber replacement:</strong> LKR 15,000-40,000 per pair</li><li><strong>Strut replacement:</strong> LKR 25,000-60,000 per pair</li><li><strong>Control arm replacement:</strong> LKR 8,000-25,000 each</li><li><strong>Complete suspension overhaul:</strong> LKR 80,000-200,000</li></ul><p>🔧 <strong>Experiencing suspension problems?</strong> Don''t let worn suspension compromise your safety and comfort. Contact Logivis for professional suspension diagnosis, repair, and upgrade services across Sri Lanka.</p>',
    status = 'published'
WHERE id = 1025;

-- Post 1026: Vehicle Air Conditioning
UPDATE public.app_post SET 
    title = 'The Complete Guide to Vehicle Air Conditioning Maintenance',
    slug = 'complete-guide-vehicle-air-conditioning-maintenance',
    description = '<h3>Keep Your Car''s AC Running Efficiently</h3><p>In Sri Lanka''s tropical climate, a properly functioning air conditioning system is essential for comfort and safety. Regular maintenance ensures optimal performance and prevents costly repairs.</p><h4>How Your Car''s AC System Works</h4><p><strong>Key Components:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Compressor:</strong> Pressurizes and circulates refrigerant</li><li><strong>Condenser:</strong> Removes heat from compressed refrigerant</li><li><strong>Evaporator:</strong> Absorbs heat from cabin air</li><li><strong>Expansion valve:</strong> Controls refrigerant flow</li><li><strong>Receiver/dryer:</strong> Filters and stores refrigerant</li></ul><p><strong>The Cooling Process:</strong></p><ol><li>Compressor pressurizes refrigerant gas</li><li>Hot, high-pressure gas flows to condenser</li><li>Condenser cools gas back to liquid</li><li>Liquid refrigerant passes through expansion valve</li><li>Low-pressure liquid evaporates in evaporator</li><li>Evaporation process absorbs heat from cabin air</li></ol><h4>Common AC Problems and Solutions</h4><p><strong>1. Insufficient Cooling</strong></p><p><strong>Causes:</strong></p><ul><li>Low refrigerant levels</li><li>Dirty air filters</li><li>Blocked condenser</li><li>Faulty compressor</li></ul><p><strong>Solutions:</strong></p><ul><li>Refrigerant recharge (every 2-3 years)</li><li>Replace cabin air filter</li><li>Clean condenser fins</li><li>Professional compressor diagnosis</li></ul><p><strong>2. Strange Odors</strong></p><p><strong>Musty smell:</strong></p><ul><li>Cause: Mold/bacteria in evaporator</li><li>Solution: Evaporator cleaning and disinfection</li><li>Prevention: Run AC regularly, use fresh air mode</li></ul><p><strong>Sweet smell:</strong></p><ul><li>Cause: Coolant leak into cabin</li><li>Solution: Immediate professional inspection</li></ul><p><strong>3. Unusual Noises</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Squealing:</strong> Worn compressor belt</li><li><strong>Grinding:</strong> Compressor bearing failure</li><li><strong>Clicking:</strong> Low refrigerant or electrical issues</li></ul><h4>Regular AC Maintenance Schedule</h4><p><strong>Monthly Checks:</strong></p><ul><li>Test AC cooling performance</li><li>Check for unusual noises or odors</li><li>Inspect cabin air filter condition</li><li>Run AC for 10 minutes to prevent seals from drying</li></ul><p><strong>Every 6 Months:</strong></p><ul><li>Replace cabin air filter</li><li>Clean condenser exterior</li><li>Check refrigerant level (professional service)</li><li>Inspect AC belts and hoses</li></ul><p><strong>Annual Service:</strong></p><ul><li>Complete AC system inspection</li><li>Refrigerant pressure test</li><li>Evaporator and condenser cleaning</li><li>Check electrical connections</li><li>Test temperature output</li></ul><h4>Refrigerant Types and Environmental Considerations</h4><p><strong>R-134a (Older Vehicles):</strong></p><ul><li>Being phased out globally</li><li>Still used in vehicles before 2017</li><li>Ozone-friendly but high global warming potential</li></ul><p><strong>R-1234yf (Newer Vehicles):</strong></p><ul><li>Environmentally friendly</li><li>Lower global warming potential</li><li>Required in newer vehicle models</li><li>More expensive but better for environment</li></ul><h4>DIY Maintenance Tips</h4><p><strong>What You Can Do:</strong></p><ul><li>Replace cabin air filter (every 6 months)</li><li>Clean condenser with compressed air</li><li>Check AC operation monthly</li><li>Keep windows cracked when parked (reduces initial heat load)</li></ul><p><strong>What Requires Professional Service:</strong></p><ul><li>Refrigerant handling and recharging</li><li>Compressor replacement</li><li>Leak detection and repair</li><li>Electrical system diagnosis</li></ul><h4>Maximizing AC Efficiency</h4><p><strong>Best Practices:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pre-cooling:</strong> Ventilate hot car before using AC</li><li><strong>Gradual cooling:</strong> Start with windows down, then close and use AC</li><li><strong>Recirculation mode:</strong> Use in city traffic, fresh air on highways</li><li><strong>Parking strategies:</strong> Use sunshades, park in shade when possible</li></ul><p><strong>Temperature Settings:</strong></p><ul><li>Optimal cabin temperature: 22-24°C</li><li>Avoid extreme cold settings (wastes fuel)</li><li>Use auto mode for consistent temperature</li></ul><h4>Fuel Economy and AC Usage</h4><p><strong>AC vs Windows Down:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>City speeds (&lt;50 km/h):</strong> Windows down more efficient</li><li><strong>Highway speeds (&gt;60 km/h):</strong> AC more efficient</li><li><strong>Average impact:</strong> AC reduces fuel economy by 5-15%</li></ul><h4>Tropical Climate Considerations</h4><p><strong>High Humidity Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Increased condensation in system</li><li>Higher risk of mold and bacteria</li><li>More frequent filter replacement needed</li></ul><p><strong>Heat Management:</strong></p><ul><li>Regular condenser cleaning essential</li><li>Parking in shade extends component life</li><li>Using window tinting reduces AC load</li></ul><h4>Warning Signs Requiring Immediate Attention</h4><ul><li><strong>No cooling at all</strong> - compressor or refrigerant issue</li><li><strong>Ice forming on evaporator</strong> - low refrigerant or airflow problem</li><li><strong>Sweet smell with AC on</strong> - possible coolant leak</li><li><strong>Loud grinding noise</strong> - compressor bearing failure</li></ul><p>❄️ <strong>AC not cooling properly in Sri Lanka''s heat?</strong> Don''t suffer in hot weather. Contact Logivis for professional AC diagnosis, repair, and maintenance services to keep you cool and comfortable year-round.</p>',
    status = 'published'
WHERE id = 1026;

-- Post 1029: Choosing Right Tires
UPDATE public.app_post SET 
    title = 'Choosing the Right Tires for Sri Lankan Road Conditions',
    slug = 'choosing-right-tires-sri-lankan-road-conditions',
    description = '<h3>Tire Selection for Sri Lankan Roads</h3><p>Sri Lanka''s diverse road conditions - from smooth highways to rough rural roads, wet monsoon conditions to hot dry weather - require careful tire selection for optimal safety, performance, and longevity.</p><h4>Understanding Sri Lankan Road Challenges</h4><p><strong>Road Surface Variations:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Expressways:</strong> Smooth asphalt, high-speed driving</li><li><strong>A-Class roads:</strong> Generally good condition, moderate traffic</li><li><strong>B-Class roads:</strong> Variable condition, potholes common</li><li><strong>Rural roads:</strong> Rough surfaces, loose gravel, dirt sections</li></ul><p><strong>Weather Conditions:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Monsoon season:</strong> Heavy rain, flooding, slippery roads</li><li><strong>Dry season:</strong> Hot pavement, increased tire wear</li><li><strong>Coastal areas:</strong> Salt air, humid conditions</li><li><strong>Hill country:</strong> Steep gradients, temperature variations</li></ul><h4>Tire Types for Different Needs</h4><p><strong>1. All-Season Tires</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Best for:</strong> General city and highway driving</li><li><strong>Pros:</strong> Good wet/dry performance, longer tread life</li><li><strong>Cons:</strong> Compromise in extreme conditions</li><li><strong>Recommended brands:</strong> Michelin Primacy, Bridgestone Ecopia, Continental ComfortContact</li></ul><p><strong>2. Touring Tires</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Highway driving, comfort-focused vehicles</li><li><strong>Pros:</strong> Quiet ride, good fuel economy, durability</li><li><strong>Cons:</strong> Limited off-road capability</li><li><strong>Recommended:</strong> Yokohama BluEarth, Dunlop SP Sport</li></ul><p><strong>3. Performance Tires</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Sports cars, enthusiast drivers</li><li><strong>Pros:</strong> Excellent grip, responsive handling</li><li><strong>Cons:</strong> Shorter tread life, road noise</li><li><strong>Recommended:</strong> Pirelli P Zero, Michelin Pilot Sport</li></ul><p><strong>4. SUV/4WD Tires</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Off-road capability, rural driving</li><li><li><strong>All-terrain:</strong> Balanced on/off-road performance</li><li><strong>Highway terrain:</strong> On-road focused for SUVs</li><li><strong>Mud-terrain:</strong> Serious off-road use</li></ul><h4>Key Features for Sri Lankan Conditions</h4><p><strong>1. Wet Weather Performance</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Deep tread grooves:</strong> Better water evacuation</li><li><strong>Silica-enhanced compound:</strong> Improved wet grip</li><li><strong>Directional tread patterns:</strong> Reduced hydroplaning risk</li><li><strong>Minimum tread depth:</strong> Replace at 3mm for safety</li></ul><p><strong>2. Heat Resistance</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Heat-resistant sidewalls:</strong> Prevent blowouts in hot weather</li><li><strong>Proper speed rating:</strong> Match vehicle requirements</li><li><strong>Load index consideration:</strong> Don''t overload tires</li></ul><p><strong>3. Durability Features</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Reinforced sidewalls:</strong> Resist pothole damage</li><li><strong>Steel belt construction:</strong> Puncture resistance</li><li><strong>Enhanced shoulder design:</strong> Even wear patterns</li></ul><h4>Tire Size and Specifications</h4><p><strong>Reading Tire Markings:</strong></p><p>Example: 205/55R16 91H</p><ul><li><strong>205:</strong> Width in millimeters</li><li><strong>55:</strong> Aspect ratio (sidewall height as % of width)</li><li><strong>R:</strong> Radial construction</li><li><strong>16:</strong> Rim diameter in inches</li><li><strong>91:</strong> Load index</li><li><strong>H:</strong> Speed rating (210 km/h maximum)</li></ul><h4>Popular Tire Brands in Sri Lanka</h4><p><strong>Premium Brands:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Michelin:</strong> Excellent longevity, fuel efficiency</li><li><strong>Bridgestone:</strong> Good all-around performance</li><li><strong>Continental:</strong> Superior wet weather performance</li><li><strong>Pirelli:</strong> Performance-oriented options</li></ul><p><strong>Mid-Range Quality:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Yokohama:</strong> Good value, reliable performance</li><li><strong>Dunlop:</strong> Balanced characteristics</li><li><strong>Toyo:</strong> Durable, good for local conditions</li><li><strong>Hankook:</strong> Competitive pricing, decent quality</li></ul><p><strong>Budget Options:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Maxxis:</strong> Affordable, adequate performance</li><li><strong>Kumho:</strong> Good entry-level choice</li><li><strong>Federal:</strong> Basic performance, low cost</li></ul><h4>Tire Maintenance for Sri Lankan Conditions</h4><p><strong>Regular Checks:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pressure monitoring:</strong> Weekly checks (heat affects pressure)</li><li><strong>Tread depth:</strong> Monthly measurements</li><li><strong>Visual inspection:</strong> Look for cuts, bulges, foreign objects</li><li><strong>Rotation schedule:</strong> Every 8,000-10,000 km</li></ul><p><strong>Monsoon Preparation:</strong></p><ul><li>Ensure adequate tread depth (minimum 3mm)</li><li>Check tire pressure regularly</li><li>Inspect for any damage before rainy season</li><li>Consider wet-weather specific tires for safety</li></ul><h4>Cost Considerations</h4><p><strong>Initial Investment vs Long-term Value:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Premium tires:</strong> Higher upfront cost, better fuel economy, longer life</li><li><strong>Budget tires:</strong> Lower initial cost, may need earlier replacement</li><li><strong>Total cost of ownership:</strong> Consider fuel efficiency and replacement intervals</li></ul><p><strong>Average Tire Prices (per tire):</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Compact cars:</strong> LKR 8,000-25,000</li><li><strong>Sedans:</strong> LKR 12,000-35,000</li><li><strong>SUVs:</strong> LKR 18,000-50,000</li><li><strong>Premium/Performance:</strong> LKR 25,000-80,000</li></ul><h4>When to Replace Tires</h4><p><strong>Safety Indicators:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tread depth below 3mm</strong></li><li><strong>Uneven wear patterns</strong></li><li><strong>Sidewall damage or bulges</strong></li><li><strong>Age over 6 years</strong> (regardless of tread)</li><li><strong>Frequent puncture repairs</strong></li></ul><p>🛞 <strong>Need help selecting the right tires for your vehicle and driving conditions?</strong> Contact Logivis for expert tire consultation, installation, and maintenance services across Sri Lanka. We''ll help you choose the perfect tires for safety and performance.</p>',
    status = 'published'
WHERE id = 1029;

-- Post 1030: Professional Vehicle Diagnostics
UPDATE public.app_post SET 
    title = 'Professional Vehicle Diagnostics: Why It Matters',
    slug = 'professional-vehicle-diagnostics-why-it-matters',
    description = '<h3>The Importance of Professional Vehicle Diagnostics</h3><p>Modern vehicles are sophisticated machines with complex electronic systems. Professional diagnostics using advanced tools can identify problems early, save money on repairs, and ensure optimal vehicle performance.</p><h4>Evolution of Vehicle Diagnostics</h4><p><strong>Traditional Methods vs Modern Diagnostics:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Past:</strong> Mechanical inspection, basic multimeters</li><li><strong>Present:</strong> Computer-based systems, bi-directional communication</li><li><strong>Future:</strong> AI-assisted diagnosis, predictive maintenance</li></ul><p><strong>Why Professional Diagnostics Matter:</strong></p><ul><li>Vehicles have 50+ electronic control units (ECUs)</li><li>Over 10,000 diagnostic trouble codes possible</li><li>Complex interconnected systems require specialized knowledge</li><li>Early detection prevents expensive component failures</li></ul><h4>Levels of Diagnostic Capability</h4><p><strong>1. Basic Code Readers</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Function:</strong> Read and clear engine codes</li><li><strong>Limitation:</strong> Surface-level information only</li><li><strong>Cost:</strong> LKR 2,000-8,000</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> DIY enthusiasts, basic troubleshooting</li></ul><p><strong>2. Mid-Level Scanners</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Function:</strong> Multiple system access, live data</li><li><strong>Features:</strong> ABS, airbag, transmission diagnostics</li><li><strong>Cost:</strong> LKR 15,000-50,000</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Independent mechanics, small shops</li></ul><p><strong>3. Professional Diagnostic Systems</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Function:</strong> Complete vehicle analysis, programming</li><li><strong>Features:</strong> Bi-directional controls, ECU coding, advanced testing</li><li><strong>Cost:</strong> LKR 100,000-500,000+</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Dealerships, specialized repair facilities</li></ul><h4>What Professional Diagnostics Can Detect</h4><p><strong>Engine and Powertrain:</strong></p><ul><li>Fuel injection system faults</li><li>Ignition system problems</li><li>Emission control issues</li><li>Transmission performance problems</li><li>Turbocharger/supercharger faults</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Systems:</strong></p><ul><li>ABS and brake system faults</li><li>Airbag system malfunctions</li><li>Electronic stability control issues</li><li>Tire pressure monitoring problems</li><li>Advanced driver assistance system (ADAS) calibration</li></ul><p><strong>Comfort and Convenience:</strong></p><ul><li>Climate control system diagnostics</li><li>Power window and lock problems</li><li>Infotainment system issues</li><li>Navigation and communication faults</li><li>Lighting system problems</li></ul><p><strong>Electrical System:</strong></p><ul><li>Charging system performance</li><li>Battery health analysis</li><li>Wiring harness continuity</li><li>Module communication errors</li><li>Power distribution faults</li></ul><h4>Advanced Diagnostic Procedures</h4><p><strong>1. Live Data Analysis</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Real-time monitoring:</strong> Engine parameters during operation</li><li><strong>Drive cycle testing:</strong> Performance under various conditions</li><li><strong>Comparative analysis:</strong> Actual vs expected values</li></ul><p><strong>2. Bi-Directional Testing</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Component activation:</strong> Test actuators and solenoids</li><li><strong>System cycling:</strong> Verify proper operation</li><li><strong>Calibration procedures:</strong> Reset learned values</li></ul><p><strong>3. Network Communication Testing</strong></p><ul><li><strong>CAN bus analysis:</strong> Check module communication</li><li><strong>Protocol verification:</strong> Ensure proper data exchange</li><li><strong>Network integrity:</strong> Identify wiring or connector issues</li></ul><h4>Benefits of Professional Diagnostics</h4><p><strong>Cost Savings:</strong></p><ul><li>Accurate diagnosis prevents unnecessary part replacement</li><li>Early detection prevents major failures</li><li>Proper repair procedures reduce comeback rates</li><li>Warranty preservation through documented diagnostics</li></ul><p><strong>Time Efficiency:</strong></p><ul><li>Quick identification of root causes</li><li>Reduced diagnostic time vs trial-and-error methods</li><li>Comprehensive system checks in single session</li><li>Proper repair procedures from first attempt</li></ul><p><strong>Safety and Reliability:</strong></p><ul><li>Detection of safety-critical system faults</li><li>Verification of repair completeness</li><li>Preventive maintenance recommendations</li><li>Performance optimization</li></ul><h4>When to Seek Professional Diagnostics</h4><p><strong>Warning Signs:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Check engine light</strong> or other warning indicators</li><li><strong>Performance issues:</strong> Poor acceleration, rough idle, stalling</li><li><strong>Fuel economy changes:</strong> Sudden increase in consumption</li><li><strong>Unusual noises:</strong> Especially electronic or electrical sounds</li><li><strong>Intermittent problems:</strong> Issues that come and go</li></ul><p><strong>Routine Maintenance:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Annual comprehensive scan</strong> for preventive maintenance</li><li><strong>Pre-purchase inspection</strong> of used vehicles</li><li><strong>Post-repair verification</strong> to ensure proper fix</li><li><strong>Performance optimization</strong> for modified vehicles</li></ul><h4>Professional Diagnostic Tools at Logivis</h4><p><strong>Launch X431 Pro V5:</strong></p><ul><li>Complete vehicle system coverage</li><li>Advanced ECU programming capabilities</li><li>Regular software updates</li><li>Comprehensive database for Asian vehicles</li></ul><p><strong>Specialized Equipment:</strong></p><ul><li>Oscilloscopes for electrical analysis</li><li>Pressure testing equipment</li><li>Advanced multimeters</li><li>Network communication analyzers</li></ul><h4>Choosing the Right Diagnostic Service</h4><p><strong>Key Factors:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Equipment quality:</strong> Professional-grade tools and regular updates</li><li><strong>Technician training:</strong> Certified and experienced diagnosticians</li><li><strong>Brand specialization:</strong> Expertise in your vehicle make</li><li><strong>Documentation:</strong> Detailed reports and repair recommendations</li><li><strong>Warranty:</strong> Stand behind diagnostic accuracy</li></ul><p><strong>Questions to Ask:</strong></p><ul><li>What diagnostic equipment do you use?</li><li>Are your technicians certified?</li><li>Do you provide written diagnostic reports?</li><li>What''s your diagnostic accuracy rate?</li><li>Do you warranty your diagnostic findings?</li></ul><h4>Cost vs Value of Professional Diagnostics</h4><p><strong>Diagnostic Fees:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Basic scan:</strong> LKR 2,000-5,000</li><li><strong>Comprehensive diagnosis:</strong> LKR 8,000-15,000</li><li><strong>Advanced troubleshooting:</strong> LKR 15,000-30,000</li><li><strong>Specialist diagnostics (hybrid/EV):</strong> LKR 20,000-50,000</li></ul><p><strong>Return on Investment:</strong></p><ul><li>Prevents misdiagnosis and unnecessary repairs</li><li>Identifies multiple issues in single session</li><li>Reduces vehicle downtime</li><li>Maintains vehicle reliability and value</li></ul><p>🔍 <strong>Experiencing unexplained vehicle problems?</strong> Don''t waste money on guesswork repairs. Contact Logivis for professional diagnostic services using the latest equipment and expert technicians across Sri Lanka.</p>',
    status = 'published'
WHERE id = 1030;